# sqlite-vec upstream pin.
#
# A SQLite loadable extension, not a server: the service loads it into its
# own process through node:sqlite. The npm `sqlite-vec` package ships
# prebuilt extensions for every platform gezel runs on except Windows ARM64,
# so this pipeline builds that one (see README.md). Keep `tag` equal to the
# npm `sqlite-vec` version pinned in packages/service/package.json, so every
# platform runs the same extension.
#
# Built from upstream's release amalgamation (sqlite-vec.c + sqlite-vec.h,
# the same source the npm prebuilds compile) against the SQLite headers
# upstream's own release workflow vendors. Both archives are pinned by
# sha256; build.ps1 refuses anything else.
#
# How to bump:
#   1. `gh api repos/asg017/sqlite-vec/git/refs/tags/<tag> --jq .object.sha`
#   2. Download `sqlite-vec-<ver>-amalgamation.tar.gz` from that release and
#      record its sha256 below.
#   3. Check upstream's scripts/vendor.sh for the SQLite amalgamation it
#      vendors; if it moved, pin the new zip and its sha256.
#   4. Run build.ps1, then `node scripts/smoke-sqlite-vec.mjs` on the
#      output, and update native/licenses/manifest.json + NOTICE.md.
#
# License: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec).
# SQLite's headers are public domain.
